Done. Here's a summary of this round's changes across 5 files:

**`GlobalHistogramBinarizer`**
- `initArrays()`: `Arrays.fill(buckets, 0)` instead of a manual loop (consistent with the prior `BitArray`/`BitMatrix` fix).

**`HybridBinarizer`**
- Added `BLOCK_SIZE_GRID = 5` and `BLOCK_SIZE_GRID_AREA = 25` constants to replace the bare `5` / `25` magic numbers that the class comment described but code never named.
- `MINIMUM_DIMENSION` now references `BLOCK_SIZE_GRID` so its intent is self-evident.
- The ceiling-division `x >> P; if (x & M != 0) x++` idiom collapsed to the equivalent one-liner `(x + BLOCK_SIZE_MASK) >> BLOCK_SIZE_POWER`.

**`GenericMultipleBarcodeReader`**
- Added a `Set<String> foundTexts` threaded through the recursive `doDecodeMultiple` call tree. Duplicate-text detection is now O(1) per result instead of an O(n) linear scan over the accumulating results list.

**`BufferedImageLuminanceSource`**
- `MINUS_45_IN_RADIANS` initializer changed from a raw literal `−0.7853981633974483` (with a comment explaining it) to `Math.toRadians(-45.0)` (self-documenting, no comment needed).

**`CommandLineRunner`**
- `expand()`: the separate second-pass loop that fixed up scheme-less URIs is merged inline into the `else` branch of the first loop — the two passes were semantically equivalent so they can be one.
- Removed trailing whitespace on the `int successful = 0;` line.

